+## Audit & Runbook Drill Playbook (High-level)
+
+Purpose
+- Ensure autonomous actions are safe, auditable and verifiable. Runbook covers weekly drills, KMS rotation dry-runs, DP sweeps, and canary drills.
+
+Preconditions
+- All secrets set (KUBE_CONFIG_DATA, EVIDENCE_BUCKET, COSIGN_KMS_URI, REKOR_SERVER, OIDC_JWKS_URL).
+- ArgoCD/Helm deployed for staging and CI runner has cosign + rekor-cli available.
+
+Weekly drill (automated)
+1) Preflight: verify secrets, kubeconfig, evidence S3 accessibility.
+2) Canary drill: execute a conservative canary promotion with a smoke image; expect Flagger to analyze.
+3) KMS dry-run: run alias rotation script in non-destructive mode (create key + alias) write manifest but DO NOT point alias in production.
+4) Privacy sweep: small dataset privacy tuning + decision manifest.
+5) Package artifacts: create audit packet and upload to evidence S3 and register with Rekor.
+6) Create issue: open a GitHub issue summarizing drill and actions.
+
+Emergency procedures
+- If canary causes blocking failures, run vwc_rollback or set ValidatingWebhookConfiguration.failurePolicy=Ignore.
+- If KMS rotation reveals IAM misconfiguration, revert alias and escalate to security team.
+
+Audit intake
+- Use ops/evidence/audit_request_generator.py to prepare packet. Deliver to auditor with scope and time-window.
+
